msgstr ""

#: src/Kits/CheckoutFields/CheckoutFieldsKit.php:90
msgid "Edits apply to both the billing and the shipping address, in every country (a country's own rules, such as no postcode, still apply to what you leave unchanged). Extra fields here are asked in both addresses. The Checkout block uses label, required, hidden and order, but not placeholders (it shows labels inside the inputs), and the country field cannot be hidden or made optional. Company, apartment and phone: required and hidden replace the visibility you set in the Checkout block's settings while this kit is on."
msgstr ""

#: src/Kits/CheckoutFields/CheckoutFieldsKit.php:97
msgid "Extra fields here appear in the Checkout block's \"Additional order information\" section and after the order notes in the classic checkout. The order notes field can only be changed in the classic checkout; in the Checkout block, switch it on or off in the block's settings."
msgstr ""

#: src/Kits/CheckoutFields/CheckoutFieldsKit.php:106
msgid "What the Checkout block cannot do"
msgstr ""

#: src/Kits/CheckoutFields/CheckoutFieldsKit.php:107
msgid "WooCommerce's Checkout block (WooCommerce 11.2) has text, dropdown, checkbox and date fields only: a text area is a one-line input there, and email, phone and number fields are text inputs that are checked when the order is placed. In the Contact and Order sections, extra fields always come after the built-in fields; address fields, built-in and extra, follow the Order numbers. Placeholders, the email field and the order notes field are classic checkout only."
